Open profile streams through wide C strings

icux::filestring is std::wstring on Windows. Constructing std::ifstream or
std::ofstream from a std::wstring is an MSVC extension; libstdc++ on Windows
provides the const wchar_t* constructors but no std::wstring ones, so
chkd_profiles.cpp stops with

    no matching function for call to
    'std::basic_ofstream<char>::basic_ofstream(icux::filestring, std::_Ios_Openmode)'

Pass .c_str() instead. map_file.cpp and lite_map_file.cpp already open their
output streams exactly this way, and MSVC accepts it too.

Upstream: not submitted yet
Applies-to: all environments

